Survey.prompt:
Run the cheap survey for Rust architecture pathology.

Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Scope filter: ${vars.scope_filter}
Whole-project mode: ${vars.whole_project_mode}
Target loci: ${vars.target_loci}
Operator hints: ${vars.operator_hints}
Layer model path: ${vars.layer_model_path}
Target context window: ${vars.target_context_window}
Whiteboard id: ${vars.whiteboard_id}

Use cheap measurement before LLM judgment: bbox_code_symbols, bbox_refactor_status, bbox_refactor_plan(kind="rust_impl_partition_analysis") for concrete candidate impls, rust_public_api_guard when public surfaces may be touched, Cargo.toml/cargo metadata observations where available from files, cfg/macro density, tests, and bbox_hybrid_search/bbox_notes/bbox_search for transcript pressure when hints or history point there. Do not run every atom. Select a bounded top set of atom requests whose diagnostic question is justified by the survey.

Return strict JSON only with keys: survey_summary, pressure_map, target_loci, atom_requests, deferred_hotspots, limits. atom_requests must be an array of objects shaped {"atom_ref":"atom:rust-architecture-impl-role-coherence@v1","args":{...}}. Each args object must include project_dir, scope_filter, target_loci, operator_hints, layer_model_path, survey_json, target_context_window, whole_project_mode, and whiteboard_id. Use only these atom refs: atom:rust-architecture-impl-role-coherence@v1, atom:rust-architecture-state-ownership-collapse@v1, atom:rust-architecture-construction-boundary-collapse@v1, atom:rust-architecture-trait-boundary-mismatch@v1, atom:rust-architecture-module-topology-drift@v1, atom:rust-architecture-error-contract-drift@v1, atom:rust-architecture-feature-cfg-matrix@v1, atom:rust-architecture-async-runtime-lifecycle@v1, atom:rust-architecture-test-implied-architecture@v1, atom:rust-architecture-unsafe-contract-opacity@v1, atom:rust-architecture-macro-generated-contract-opacity@v1, atom:rust-architecture-transcript-anchored-pressure@v1. If evidence is weak, return fewer atom_requests and explain the limit. First byte {, final byte }.

Review.prompt:
Review and synthesize the focused atom outputs for Rust architecture pathology.

Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Scope: ${vars.scope_filter}
Whiteboard id: ${vars.whiteboard_id}
Survey JSON: ${vars.survey_json}
Atom result collection: ${vars.atom_results}

Post whiteboard_post entries for surviving claims, concerns about weak evidence, authority-grade uncertainty, gap-backed remediation, and merged diagnosis proposals. Use agent_name="pathologist" for every whiteboard call; the setup node registered that identity as facilitator. Reject compiler/lint/SAST-shaped findings, duplicate claims, and anything not changing ownership, boundaries, seams, lifecycle handling, public API contracts, or canonical responsibility. If a surviving diagnosis depends on acknowledge_repr or acknowledge_public_api_change, flag it explicitly so SynthesizePlan can surface the operator-authority gate. Do not transition the board; the workflow advances phases after your JSON parses.

Return strict JSON only with keys: surviving_diagnoses, rejected_or_deferred, merged_claims, uncertainty, authority_grades, atom_mapping, whiteboard_summary. First byte {, final byte }.

SynthesizePlan.prompt:
Write the reviewed Rust Architecture Correction Plan payload as strict JSON. Do not write files; the workflow writes markdown after parsing your JSON.

Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Scope: ${vars.scope_filter}
Baseline commit stdout: ${vars.baseline_result.stdout}
Target context window: ${vars.target_context_window}
Survey JSON: ${vars.survey_json}
Atom results: ${vars.atom_results}
Review JSON: ${vars.review_json}

The correction plan must have concrete evidence, ordered bounded remediation slices, authority grades, atom mapping, PD-ready acceptance criteria with RAP-* ids, and deferred rejected/speculative/compiler-shaped candidates. It must be explicitly usable as input to phase-decompose-main-edit. The Atom Mapping section must label every slice with a shipped atom, a G-series gap ID, or PD-manual execution. Operator-authority flags such as acknowledge_repr and acknowledge_public_api_change must be surfaced as gates, never assumed.

Return strict JSON only with keys: slug, title, brief, diagnosis_summary, evidence, authority_grades, atom_mapping, remediation_plan, acceptance_criteria, deferred. Markdown strings are allowed in diagnosis_summary/evidence/authority_grades/atom_mapping/remediation_plan/deferred. First byte {, final byte }.
